<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isatay Taimanuly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1791">1791</a>–<a href="/years/1838">1838</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Isatay Taymanov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isatay Taimanuly was a Kazakh batyr and elder of the Bukey Horde who led a revolt from 1836 to 1838 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jangir-khan">Jangir Khan</a> and the Russian-backed elite. Together with the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makhambet-otemisuly">Makhambet Otemisuly</a> he protested the khan's land grants and heavy exactions on ordinary herders. The rising was suppressed with the help of Russian troops, and Isatay was killed in battle in 1838. He is remembered in Kazakhstan as a national hero.</p></div>
